WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:14.840
Pinocchio was so happy he couldn't sleep!

2
00:00:14.841 --> 00:00:17.421
Tomorrow was his first day of school.

3
00:00:17.422 --> 00:00:20.370
He thought about the wonderful things he would learn.

4
00:00:20.371 --> 00:00:27.317
When the sun came up, he jumped out of bed, grabbed his new book, and ran off to school.

5
00:00:27.318 --> 00:00:32.164
"Bye, Father!" he shouted.

6
00:00:32.165 --> 00:00:35.105
Pinocchio talked to himself happily as he walked.

7
00:00:35.106 --> 00:00:37.445
"Today, I will learn to read.

8
00:00:37.446 --> 00:00:39.957
Tomorrow, I will learn to write.

9
00:00:39.958 --> 00:00:43.773
And the day after tomorrow, I will learn math.

10
00:00:43.774 --> 00:00:47.824
I will be so smart!

11
00:00:47.825 --> 00:00:52.211
I will be smart enough to get a job and earn money.

12
00:00:52.212 --> 00:00:54.814
I will buy Father a new coat.

13
00:00:54.815 --> 00:01:00.932
It will be a beautiful coat of green silk with diamond buttons.

14
00:01:00.933 --> 00:01:04.863
He was very kind to sell his coat for this book."

15
00:01:04.864 --> 00:01:10.579
As he talked to himself, he heard music in the distance.

16
00:01:10.580 --> 00:01:16.643
He walked toward the music and saw a crowd, a brightly colored tent, and a large sign.

17
00:01:16.644 --> 00:01:20.548
"Oh! I wish I didn't have to go to school today!

18
00:01:20.549 --> 00:01:24.731
This looks like so much fun," complained Pinocchio.

19
00:01:24.732 --> 00:01:28.471
Already, he had forgotten Geppetto's coat.

20
00:01:28.472 --> 00:01:32.258
"Excuse me," Pinocchio said to one of the villagers.

21
00:01:32.259 --> 00:01:34.721
"What does that sign say?"

22
00:01:34.722 --> 00:01:41.618
"Why? Can't you read?" the villager asked, laughing.

23
00:01:41.619 --> 00:01:46.083
"No," said Pinocchio, embarrassed.

24
00:01:46.084 --> 00:01:50.996
"It says 'Fettuccini's Marionette Theater, four lire.'

25
00:01:50.997 --> 00:01:53.358
The show starts in five minutes.

26
00:01:53.359 --> 00:01:55.081
But you can't read.

27
00:01:55.082 --> 00:01:57.627
You should be in school."

28
00:01:57.628 --> 00:02:01.856
"I don't want to go to school!" Pinocchio cried.

29
00:02:01.857 --> 00:02:05.411
"Do you have four lire I can borrow?"

30
00:02:05.412 --> 00:02:07.836
Pinocchio was embarrassed to beg.

31
00:02:07.837 --> 00:02:10.204
But he really wanted to see the show.

32
00:02:10.205 --> 00:02:13.778
"I have four lire," the villager said.

33
00:02:13.779 --> 00:02:16.139
"But it's not for borrowing.

34
00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:18.917
You have to sell me something."

35
00:02:18.918 --> 00:02:25.285
"But, I have nothing except my clothes and this book!" Pinocchio cried.

36
00:02:25.286 --> 00:02:29.089
"Then I'll take your book," the villager said.

37
00:02:29.090 --> 00:02:31.697
He knew the book cost more than four lire.

38
00:02:31.698 --> 00:02:36.155
Pinocchio took the money.

39
00:02:36.156 --> 00:02:38.245
Pinocchio ran inside the tent.

40
00:02:38.246 --> 00:02:40.861
The flute and drums played a new song.

41
00:02:40.862 --> 00:02:43.841
A few marionettes were brought out to dance.

42
00:02:43.842 --> 00:02:49.926
"Hey, they are wooden boys just like me!" Pinocchio said excitedly.

43
00:02:49.927 --> 00:02:53.953
He ran to the stage to look closer.

44
00:02:53.954 --> 00:02:56.541
"But wait. They aren't real!

45
00:02:56.542 --> 00:02:58.891
They are dancing with strings!

46
00:02:58.892 --> 00:03:05.034
I can dance better than that, and I don't need strings or a hiding man to pull them!"

47
00:03:05.035 --> 00:03:08.790
Pinocchio jumped on stage with the marionettes and shouted,

48
00:03:08.791 --> 00:03:13.969
"I am the amazing Pinocchio."

49
00:03:13.970 --> 00:03:18.704
He danced and twirled and jumped and flipped.

50
00:03:18.705 --> 00:03:23.738
The crowd laughed and cheered. "Yeah, Pinocchio!

51
00:03:23.739 --> 00:03:26.774
You're the best puppet ever!"

52
00:03:26.775 --> 00:03:28.790
Suddenly, the music stopped.

53
00:03:28.791 --> 00:03:33.001
A man came from behind the stage and grabbed Pinocchio.

54
00:03:33.002 --> 00:03:36.450
"The show's over, folks!" he said.

55
00:03:36.451 --> 00:03:41.717
"If you want to see the amazing Pinocchio, you have to pay for another show!"

56
00:03:41.718 --> 00:03:44.387
He pulled Pinocchio behind the stage.

57
00:03:44.388 --> 00:03:52.113
"Help, help!" Pinocchio cried. "Please! Help me!"

58
00:03:52.114 --> 00:03:55.984
Pinocchio was scared of this big man with the angry voice.

59
00:03:55.985 --> 00:03:59.426
"You are mine now, little puppet.

60
00:03:59.427 --> 00:04:02.440
You will make me a lot of money.

61
00:04:02.441 --> 00:04:05.897
A puppet with no strings! Ha!"

62
00:04:05.898 --> 00:04:10.957
The man began to imagine the piles of money.

63
00:04:10.958 --> 00:04:14.081
"Please, sir. I'm Geppetto's son.

64
00:04:14.082 --> 00:04:16.010
I need to go to school.

65
00:04:16.011 --> 00:04:19.541
Please let me go," Pinocchio begged.

66
00:04:19.542 --> 00:04:21.919
"You, someone's son?

67
00:04:21.920 --> 00:04:24.569
And a school boy? Ha!

68
00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:26.604
That's a good joke.

69
00:04:26.605 --> 00:04:30.788
We will leave town so Geppetto can't find you."

70
00:04:30.789 --> 00:04:33.430
The big man locked Pinocchio in a cage.

71
00:04:33.431 --> 00:04:36.719
He hid the cage under some blankets in his wagon.

72
00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:40.621
"Now, no one can find you," the man said, laughing.

73
00:04:40.622 --> 00:04:42.513
He packed up his tent.

74
00:04:42.514 --> 00:04:47.598
"Oh, Father, I'm so sorry," cried Pinocchio.

75
00:04:47.599 --> 00:04:49.377
"Please, save me!

76
00:04:49.378 --> 00:04:59.908
I want my father. Whaaaaa."
